    metric: minimum squared Euclidean distance from any marker pixel of that color to any grey pixel
    winner: unique color with smallest distance; gap to second-best >= 2
  output: black grid with grey object repainted in winning color; all markers erased

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 2-3 marker colors + grey; all distinct, non-black.
    2. Place a symmetric grey object (4-13 pixels) near grid center.
    3. Designate one color as winner. Place 1-6 winner-color marker pixels
       with min squared distance D_win to grey (D_win >= 1).
    4. For each remaining color, place 1-6 marker pixels ensuring their
       min squared distance to grey > D_win (gap >= 2). Reject if tie.
    5. Verify all markers are isolated (no same-color 4-adjacency) and
       not on/adjacent-to grey. The output is the grey mask repainted with winner color.
